s>KI</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Medical evaluation of psychiatric patients: Results in a state mental health system</article-title><source>Arch Gen Psychiatry</source><year>1989</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>740</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2787623</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-wjem-10-97"><label>7.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dolan</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Mushlin</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Routine laboratory testing for medical disorders in psychiatric patients</article-title><source>Arc Intern Med</source><year>1985</year><volume>145</volume><fpage>2085</fpage><lpage>2088</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-wjem-10-97"><label>8.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Korn</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Currier</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medical clearance of psychiatric patients without medical complaints in the emergency department</article-title><source>J Emerg Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10699517</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-wjem-10-97"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reeves</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pendarvis</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimble</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Unrecognized Medical Emergencies Admitted to the Psychiatric Units</article-title><source>American J of Emerg Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>390</fpage><lpage>393</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-wjem-10-97"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tintinalli</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Peacock</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Emergency medical evaluation of psychiatric patients</article-title><source>Ann Emerg Med</source><year>1994</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>859</fpage><lpage>862</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8161059</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-wjem-10-97"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riba</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hale</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medical clearance: fact or fiction in the hospital emergency room</article-title><source>Psychosomatic</source><year>1990</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>400</fpage><lpage>404</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-wjem-10-97"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colgan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolle</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>McGlone</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hooton</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Asymptomatic bacteriuria in adults</article-title><source>Am Fam Physician</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>985</fpage><lpage>990</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17002033</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-wjem-10-97"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicolle</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Bradley</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Clogan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Infectious Diseases Society of America guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of asymptomatic bacteriuria in adults</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><year>2005</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15714408</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-wjem-10-97"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>U. S. Preventative Services Task Force</collab><article-title>Screening for asymptomatic bacteriuria in adults: U.S. Preventive Service Task Force Reaffirmation Recommendation Statement</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2008</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>47</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18591636</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-wjem-10-97" position="float"><label>Figure 1.</label><caption><p>Flowchart of study patients</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="wjem-10-97f1"/></fig></floats-group></article>